1149
01:43:47,992 --> 01:43:51,837
I think I saw maybe one diver looked OK.

1150
01:43:52,676 --> 01:43:58,083
He's putting his body through quite a testing and troubling build up.

1151
01:44:00,087 --> 01:44:04,011
Now 14 year old Matthew Dixon from Plymouth.

1152
01:44:06,194 --> 01:44:07,055
Great to have him here.

1153
01:44:08,396 --> 01:44:13,203
And great to see what he can do on this forward three and a half somersaults with Pike.

1154
01:44:13,684 --> 01:44:16,186
3.0 for the young man.

1155
01:44:18,791 --> 01:44:22,194
His best marks, by the way, 398.25.

1156
01:44:23,778 --> 01:44:28,565
Oh, he's a little bit short of vertical, but he does get that rip entry.

1157
01:44:29,146 --> 01:44:31,250
Bit of a crowd favourite here, and I'm not surprised.

1158
01:44:32,070 --> 01:44:36,458
Just tiny, his head is only just above the bars, the safety bars up on the 10 metre.

1159
01:44:36,918 --> 01:44:41,627
As you see clearly, as you see on the replay, the judges of course do not see the replay.

1160
01:44:41,646 --> 01:44:45,313
He enters the water short of vertical, so the marks will reflect that.

1161
01:44:46,407 --> 01:44:48,769
49.5 for Matt.

1162
01:44:49,449 --> 01:44:55,015
Whereas it was 60 this morning, so he's 11 points down on how he started in the prelims.

1163
01:44:56,756 --> 01:45:03,804
Chu Yue has, like some of the other Malaysian divers, actually been a bit of a mixed bag this week.

1164
01:45:04,125 --> 01:45:04,925
He's really on it.

1165
01:45:05,126 --> 01:45:06,646
He's really on it and gets big marks.

1166
01:45:07,528 --> 01:45:11,872
He too starts with a forward three and a half somersaults with Pike, 3.0.

1167
01:45:11,992 --> 01:45:15,756
A couple of other divers will do this one too.

1168
01:45:16,411 --> 01:45:22,520
Nice from Chu Yue, looking for that vertical entry, splashless, and he gets exactly that.

1169
01:45:22,541 --> 01:45:24,264
He's a little bit ragged.

1170
01:45:25,826 --> 01:45:29,953
Mind you, he gets into that pike shape eventually, but his form is good.

1171
01:45:29,972 --> 01:45:32,096
He's going to get eights on that, which is excellent.

1172
01:45:32,117 --> 01:45:38,006
I've been watching him on his other dives, and he tends to be a little bit here and there, but that's a solid start.

1173
01:45:38,027 --> 01:45:40,730
72 for Chu Yue.

1174
01:45:41,167 --> 01:45:43,168
One of two Malaysians in the final.

1175
01:45:43,689 --> 01:45:45,771
Coach is saying where that can improve.

1176
01:45:46,132 --> 01:45:49,337
Perhaps we can improve for the remaining five rounds as well.

1177
01:45:51,399 --> 01:45:54,283
Now this man started like a train this morning.

1178
01:45:54,302 --> 01:46:00,088
His opening dive, the armstand back double somersault to an arm twist we're about to see.

1179
01:46:00,109 --> 01:46:01,832
Looked very, very impressive.

1180
01:46:03,654 --> 01:46:04,795
See what we can do with this one.

1181
01:46:41,225 --> 01:46:42,967
Oh, it's nearly as good as the prelim.

1182
01:46:43,347 --> 01:46:44,829
That's a huge dive to open with.

1183
01:46:44,850 --> 01:46:47,875
He got massive 91 on this in the prelim.

1184
01:46:48,216 --> 01:46:49,837
He isn't going to be far away from that now.

1185
01:46:49,858 --> 01:46:51,761
This will get mid-80s somewhere.

1186
01:46:51,900 --> 01:46:53,283
It's 3.6 degree of difficulty.

1187
01:46:53,604 --> 01:46:54,484
He's going to get eights.

1188
01:46:54,505 --> 01:46:56,828
A little bit too much splash being thrown up for nines.

1189
01:46:57,510 --> 01:47:02,076
Dominic Bedgood opens his campaign with a very good dive.

1190
01:47:02,617 --> 01:47:07,224
86.4 for Dominic Bedgood.

1191
01:47:08,506 --> 01:47:10,488
14 points clear to UE.

1192
01:47:12,072 --> 01:47:15,936
And that takes him with 49.5 in third place currently.

1193
01:47:19,280 --> 01:47:19,980
So he does, Helen.

1194
01:47:20,462 --> 01:47:24,126
Looking forward to two more English divers to come.

1195
01:47:24,487 --> 01:47:26,529
James Denny up in a couple.

1196
01:47:26,930 --> 01:47:31,734
And Tom Daley, because he was the best qualifier this morning, will go last.

1197
01:47:31,756 --> 01:47:37,202
So here's Li Fengyang, now of New Zealand, formerly of China, forward three and a half.

1198
01:47:38,565 --> 01:47:40,609
Oh, just letting the dive run away.

1199
01:47:40,628 --> 01:47:42,131
The takeoff was good.

1200
01:47:42,150 --> 01:47:47,179
Probably a little bit too much forward momentum, so he moves away from the diving board quite considerably.

1201
01:47:47,698 --> 01:47:50,923
This can make controlling the dive a little bit more challenging.

1202
01:47:50,944 --> 01:47:53,467
He comes out with plenty of time just rolling over there.

1203
01:47:53,747 --> 01:47:55,329
A little bit of splash being thrown up.

1204
01:47:56,091 --> 01:48:01,418
So 3.0, relatively low degree of difficulty compared to some of the dives in his repertoire.

1205
01:48:02,060 --> 01:48:03,983
And he's a little bit off the pace.

1206
01:48:03,962 --> 01:48:04,724
58.5.

1207
01:48:05,425 --> 01:48:07,006
Sticks him in behind Bedgood.

1208
01:48:07,027 --> 01:48:12,693
Once again, a strong opening for the Australian, who you saw as we were joining.

1209
01:48:12,712 --> 01:48:13,993
Chuyue in second place.

1210
01:48:14,635 --> 01:48:18,960
Now James Denny, second of the Englishman.

1211
01:48:18,979 --> 01:48:21,483
Ninth of the Europeans on the 10-meter board.

1212
01:48:21,502 --> 01:48:22,965
Got over 400 points with it.

1213
01:48:22,984 --> 01:48:28,270
That is the silver medalist on the platform at the British Championships earlier this year.

1214
01:48:29,231 --> 01:48:30,592
And he will start with a 3.2.

1215
01:48:30,793 --> 01:48:33,716
Nice opening gambit for James.

1216
01:48:34,608 --> 01:48:40,264
In with three and a half somersaults with Tuck for the second of three Englishmen and you know who comes third.

1217
01:48:54,756 --> 01:49:00,324
Oh, there's a good start from James Denny, really clean on the water, just a little bit short as he goes in.

1218
01:49:00,604 --> 01:49:02,828
In fact, he doesn't quite straighten out enough.

1219
01:49:02,847 --> 01:49:05,192
Take off his good, squeezing into that tuck shake.

1220
01:49:05,212 --> 01:49:06,353
Three and a half somersaults.

1221
01:49:06,774 --> 01:49:10,920
Pikes out, has a good look at the water, but you see that he's got his backside sticking out as he goes in.

1222
01:49:11,501 --> 01:49:17,810
He won't get more than sevens for that, which is a shame, because if he'd have straightened out completely, he'd have been getting eights, maybe even more.

1223
01:49:18,289 --> 01:49:19,532
Seven, seven, seven.

1224
01:49:19,511 --> 01:49:23,595
On a 3.2 DD, we have DDD here.

1225
01:49:24,036 --> 01:49:30,122
Denny, Daly and Dixon.

1226
01:49:32,184 --> 01:49:34,407
Utin Yang of Malaysia.

1227
01:49:35,327 --> 01:49:39,992
Already showing what he can do on the three metre board by going on to win it.

1228
01:49:40,011 --> 01:49:43,655
And absolutely a few English hearts, not least of all, Jack Law.

1229
01:49:44,817 --> 01:49:46,177
Going from three to ten.

1230
01:49:47,103 --> 01:49:53,038
I haven't quite put in the performance yet to suggest he's a medalist, but it's the final now, not the prelims.

1231
01:49:53,078 --> 01:49:53,962
This is where it really matters.

1232
01:49:54,002 --> 01:49:58,193
Back two and a half somersaults, one and a half twists in the pike position, 3.2.

1233
01:50:00,670 --> 01:50:02,212
Yeah, dive very well this morning.

1234
01:50:02,231 --> 01:50:05,997
Utsi Liang made one mistake, which is why he's middle of the pack.

1235
01:50:06,037 --> 01:50:10,725
Divers dive in reverse order from the standings in the prelim.

1236
01:50:10,744 --> 01:50:12,127
This is good for Utsi Liang, 3.2.

1237
01:50:12,266 --> 01:50:19,176
It's actually a relatively easy twist in comparison to what you're going to see Mitchum, Daley and Denny try.

1238
01:50:19,197 --> 01:50:21,239
The back two and a half somersaults, two and a half twists.

1239
01:50:21,260 --> 01:50:23,944
This is the two and a half somersaults, one and a half twists.

1240
01:50:24,364 --> 01:50:26,087
It's worked out okay for Ooh.

1241
01:50:28,311 --> 01:50:29,632
The marks we wait for.

1242
01:50:30,394 --> 01:50:37,181
The judge is either indecisive or the technology is letting us down at the moment, so we can't bring you what he's got as yet.

1243
01:50:37,381 --> 01:50:40,706
It will be appearing on your screen.

1244
01:50:40,725 --> 01:50:43,127
Oh no, we have a judge who's not pushed their button properly.

1245
01:50:43,788 --> 01:50:46,912
So they have to re-input it before we can bring you all the scores.

1246
01:50:46,931 --> 01:50:52,057
Remember, only the middle three will count towards the total, 7.5s and 8s.

1247
01:50:53,404 --> 01:50:56,448
Did have a question about why all the marks are not counted.

1248
01:50:56,909 --> 01:50:58,011
It's about finding the average.

1249
01:50:58,072 --> 01:51:01,697
So the two highest and two lowest are discounted to get the average scores.

1250
01:51:01,737 --> 01:51:05,922
Otherwise the subjectivity plays too much of a part if all the marks count.

1251
01:51:05,943 --> 01:51:12,551
So seven judges, two highs, two lows removed and three count multiplied by the degree of difficulty gives you total for the dive.

1252
01:51:13,634 --> 01:51:14,194
Easy as that.

1253
01:51:14,876 --> 01:51:15,515
Straightforward.

1254
01:51:16,077 --> 01:51:17,739
Much more straightforward than doing the dives.

1255
01:51:18,541 --> 01:51:21,505
Forward three and a half somersaults with Mike for Ruriendo.

1256
01:51:22,666 --> 01:51:29,237
I was very impressed with Vincent Riando and next up Max Bouchard, both of these young Canadians.

1257
01:51:29,698 --> 01:51:31,902
Vincent is certainly young, 17 years old.

1258
01:51:32,502 --> 01:51:33,885
He's got a bright future in front of him.

1259
01:51:33,904 --> 01:51:36,048
This is his easiest eye, 3.0.

1260
01:51:37,110 --> 01:51:41,518
He certainly starts his campaign off in pretty steady style.

1261
01:51:42,207 --> 01:52:02,172
need six dives six consistently good dives to be anywhere near the medals let's see how this young man gets on well if we presume it will be daily at mitcham going head to head somebody needs to claim the bronze could easily be vincent riendo let's uh just come out of world juniors maybe his 10th in australia

1262
01:52:02,795 --> 01:52:07,002
Maxime Bouchard retired after 2008 World Juniors in Germany.

1263
01:52:07,542 --> 01:52:11,569
Didn't think he could cut the mustard, but it's been persuaded to come back.

1264
01:52:11,609 --> 01:52:14,012
He's kind of held together with sticky tape.

1265
01:52:14,033 --> 01:52:15,595
There's a lot of metal in that body.

1266
01:52:16,136 --> 01:52:19,440
Arm stand back, triple somersault with tuck.

1267
01:52:19,461 --> 01:52:23,106
3.3, there'll be different variances of the arm stand, we'll see.

1268
01:52:25,369 --> 01:52:27,113
Some people like to do it with a towel.

1269
01:52:27,713 --> 01:52:28,574
Some people do not.

1270
01:52:29,777 --> 01:52:30,979
Maxime is one of those.

1271
01:52:40,831 --> 01:52:45,542
Oh.

1272
01:52:45,561 --> 01:52:48,509
Well, my ooh was because he wasn't meant to do that.

1273
01:52:48,708 --> 01:52:51,354
Had a little bit of a wobble in the arm stand balance there.

1274
01:52:52,597 --> 01:52:56,847
Lost his balance, manages to hold himself, but then when he goes eventually,

1275
01:52:57,114 --> 01:53:07,864
His takeoff isn't quite as strong as it normally is, and so as he exits the dive, he thinks he's lower to the water, arches through to try and pull it in, but it's an error, and he over-rotates.

1276
01:53:08,626 --> 01:53:13,871
It's not disastrous, but it wasn't as strong as I've seen in training from Maxim.

1277
01:53:14,952 --> 01:53:20,676
In an event and a competition of this quality, anything below sevens is not going to help your medal prospects.

1278
01:53:20,697 --> 01:53:25,721
6.5 just puts him a little bit behind the pace in round one, about behind.

1279
01:53:26,021 --> 01:53:32,350
Bedgood, Buzi Liang, Chu Yue, Vincent Riando and James Denny.

1280
01:53:34,292 --> 01:53:37,917
Only ahead for the moment of Lee Dixon.

1281
01:53:38,398 --> 01:53:42,302
Not Lee Dixon obviously, Lee and Dixon.

1282
01:53:42,323 --> 01:53:43,264
I don't think he's diving yet.

1283
01:53:44,385 --> 01:53:47,088
It's a new pairing of Gary Lilica and Lee Dixon on the board.

1284
01:53:47,168 --> 01:53:51,895
Now a little chat with the Canadian coach about something there, Leon.

1285
01:53:55,181 --> 01:53:56,104
Yeah, let's wait and see.

1286
01:53:57,365 --> 01:54:00,690
I don't have any microphones down there.

1287
01:54:00,711 --> 01:54:01,591
That was the referee.

1288
01:54:03,655 --> 01:54:06,980
There was a discussion.

1289
01:54:09,666 --> 01:54:11,689
I have no idea what was discussed.

1290
01:54:12,563 --> 01:54:17,207
If you are going to make a protest, you need to make a protest straight away that maybe the referee turned it down.

1291
01:54:17,228 --> 01:54:18,149
We'll find out afterwards.

1292
01:54:18,750 --> 01:54:19,930
So there's a little disruption.

1293
01:54:19,951 --> 01:54:21,493
Now the competition really starts.

1294
01:54:21,773 --> 01:54:22,934
The head-to-head.

1295
01:54:22,953 --> 01:54:24,716
Mitchum versus Daly, take two.

1296
01:54:24,836 --> 01:54:26,417
Four years ago, it was Daly.

1297
01:54:27,038 --> 01:54:28,801
Who will it be this evening?

1298
01:54:28,961 --> 01:54:35,807
Well, I'll try and do, if I remember, is give you their marks this morning so you can compare how they've done tonight.

1299
01:54:35,828 --> 01:54:39,431
81 on the forward three and a half somersaults for Matt Mitchum this morning.

1300
01:54:41,199 --> 01:54:42,725
Oh, there you go.

1301
01:54:43,126 --> 01:54:44,591
The pressure beginning to tell.

1302
01:54:44,610 --> 01:54:47,560
Did the delay cause him to lose concentration?

1303
01:54:47,601 --> 01:54:49,387
Because that is an error for Mitchum.

1304
01:54:49,408 --> 01:54:51,935
His easiest dive and he's fluffed it.

1305
01:54:52,996 --> 01:54:55,439
Their door is wide open.

1306
01:54:56,078 --> 01:55:02,546
You cannot start your campaign with like a 60-pointer, not when you're taking on Tom Daley.

1307
01:55:02,567 --> 01:55:04,788
What are we going to see this evening?

1308
01:55:04,809 --> 01:55:07,011
6.5s is what you see there.

1309
01:55:07,471 --> 01:55:11,457
And that is some 23 points down on what he did this morning.

1310
01:55:11,676 --> 01:55:20,926
So already a big amount of ground to make up for the gold medalist from Beijing 2008, silver medalist four years ago in Delhi.

1311
01:55:21,632 --> 01:55:25,997
And the winner on the synchro last night with Dominic Bedgood.

1312
01:55:26,016 --> 01:55:28,838
So Tom Daly, arm stand to start.

1313
01:55:29,259 --> 01:55:32,002
Slightly different version of it from what we've seen thus far.

1314
01:55:32,962 --> 01:55:34,623
Arm stand back triple somersault.

1315
01:55:34,963 --> 01:55:39,648
Now when he performed this dive in the preliminaries this morning, 73.50.

1316
01:55:41,088 --> 01:55:46,194
Just to give you a little heads up, the dive he has a problem with is coming next.

1317
01:55:46,213 --> 01:55:51,537
73.5 though on his arm stand back triple this morning.

1318
01:55:58,792 --> 01:56:00,594
Hello Tom Daley!

1319
01:56:00,974 --> 01:56:04,717
Welcome to the men's 10 meter platform final.

1320
01:56:04,738 --> 01:56:07,060
This is the defending champion.

1321
01:56:07,079 --> 01:56:12,586
That is his first dive and he's gonna get nines and maybe even some tens.

1322
01:56:13,025 --> 01:56:16,088
He has capitalized on Mitchum leaving the door open.

1323
01:56:16,489 --> 01:56:19,893
Tom Daley has absolutely smashed it.

1324
01:56:19,912 --> 01:56:21,154
90 points plus.

1325
01:56:21,395 --> 01:56:22,555
Beautiful dive.

1326
01:56:23,837 --> 01:56:24,698
Game on.

1327
01:56:26,364 --> 01:56:27,768
Should we just stop the competition there?

1328
01:56:27,787 --> 01:56:30,814
94.5 compared to 73.5.

1329
01:56:30,873 --> 01:56:33,479
What a massive swing.

1330
01:56:33,498 --> 01:56:34,841
23 points down, Mitcham.

1331
01:56:35,564 --> 01:56:37,006
21 points up, Daly.

1332
01:56:37,868 --> 01:56:41,936
Swing of 44 points on one dive from this morning to evening.

1333
01:56:42,197 --> 01:56:42,757
And there it is.

1334
01:56:43,659 --> 01:56:45,082
You don't even see.

1335
01:56:46,126 --> 01:56:48,270
Matthew Mitchell in the frame there.

1336
01:56:48,890 --> 01:56:49,752
He's on page two.

1337
01:56:50,212 --> 01:56:50,833
That's good.

1338
01:56:50,854 --> 01:56:52,457
Starting well again for Australia.

1339
01:56:52,756 --> 01:56:58,286
We're having problems with a photography problem that we had in London.

1340
01:56:58,867 --> 01:57:00,930
Everyone wants to get a snapshot of Tom Daly.

1341
01:57:01,912 --> 01:57:04,556
We know how it affected his diving in London.

1342
01:57:05,018 --> 01:57:07,662
So the crowd just being told to turn those flashes off.

1343
01:57:08,805 --> 01:57:17,878
Tom Daly has a lead of eight points already and maybe more importantly has a lead of some 36 over Matt Mitchell after round one.

1344
01:57:19,421 --> 01:57:26,051
Now we're a little bit concerned for this young man because we saw him in practice tonight in training and warm up and he wasn't getting anything right.

1345
01:57:26,070 --> 01:57:28,594
Let's hope he gets through his six unscathed.

1346
01:57:29,475 --> 01:57:32,680
Inward three and a half somersaults with tuck for Siddharth Bhadeshi.

1347
01:57:32,699 --> 01:57:36,265
This is his big dive of the program at three point two.

1348
01:57:47,264 --> 01:57:49,967
Well, Siddhartha was, well, he was almost there.

1349
01:57:50,188 --> 01:57:51,710
All the components were in the right place.

1350
01:57:51,729 --> 01:57:54,132
His takeoff is good enough.

1351
01:57:55,375 --> 01:57:58,719
Good jump, good extension from the legs, moving a safe distance from the diving board.

1352
01:57:58,819 --> 01:58:02,744
Spots the water, just isn't quite confident enough to straighten out quick enough.

1353
01:58:03,225 --> 01:58:09,894
He still hits the water a little bit loose, a little bit soft, and therefore won't get more than the marks coming up.

1354
01:58:09,953 --> 01:58:11,777
Fives, 5.5s is about right.

1355
01:58:11,837 --> 01:58:15,702
If he was a bit more confident on the exit of the dive, he could even get 7s.

1356
01:58:16,087 --> 01:58:27,659
I'll be interested to see what he does in the remaining dives because what he was doing this morning taking about 25-30 seconds over each dive and it seemed to be counterproductive as he was trying to get himself prepared for it.

1357
01:58:27,680 --> 01:58:32,466
It seemed to be too much thinking and execution of the dives was suffering because of it.

1358
01:58:33,346 --> 01:58:45,621
14 year old Matt Dixon, one of the European juniors now stepping up to the senior ranks with a reverse two and a half somersaults with tuck only 2.8 degree of difficulty so

1359
01:58:45,988 --> 01:58:47,212
keeping up with the others.

1360
01:58:47,613 --> 01:58:50,680
This needs to be very good for the young man.

1361
01:58:57,917 --> 01:58:59,962
Oh, it's a tremendous entry into the water.

1362
01:59:00,603 --> 01:59:03,390
He's just a little bit untidy.

1363
01:59:03,538 --> 01:59:06,222
As he gets in, I'll tell you through it on the replay.

1364
01:59:06,243 --> 01:59:07,083
The jump is good.

1365
01:59:07,425 --> 01:59:08,405
He's only tiny, is he?

1366
01:59:08,445 --> 01:59:09,408
14 years old.

1367
01:59:09,547 --> 01:59:14,173
Spots the water, kicks out, looks over his toes, reaches back, just tipped his feet over with him.

1368
01:59:14,194 --> 01:59:15,596
So he got eight and a halfs on this earlier.

1369
01:59:15,636 --> 01:59:17,479
I think this will only get seven and a halfs.

1370
01:59:18,239 --> 01:59:19,823
