And then eventually points his toes.

1626
02:16:20,796 --> 02:16:21,797
Good entry to the water.

1627
02:16:21,837 --> 02:16:24,421
Marginally short vertical, but much, much better.

1628
02:16:24,863 --> 02:16:27,407
It's the best of the back three and a halfs in the tuck position.

1629
02:16:27,887 --> 02:16:29,690
And we've just seen three in a row.

1630
02:16:30,667 --> 02:16:34,512
Even at this stage, the minor medals are definitely up for grabs.

1631
02:16:36,315 --> 02:16:40,820
Tom Daly needs to keep the consistency going for the gold, because he's going to be untouchable if he does.

1632
02:16:41,621 --> 02:16:51,334
But silver and bronze, not out of the range of anybody in the top order at the moment, including this young man, James Denny.

1633
02:16:52,877 --> 02:16:56,162
We'll go with the same dive we've seen, but in a slightly different form.

1634
02:16:57,243 --> 02:16:58,665
Goes from tuck to pike.

1635
02:17:01,447 --> 02:17:15,760
next time by the way there's one that i've seen on youtube with no splash but uh it's gonna be very hard for this to be uh splashless mac three and a half pike big tariff 3.6 for james denny

1636
02:17:18,506 --> 02:17:22,593
Well, that's what him and Tom, one of the dives they used last night in the synchro.

1637
02:17:23,295 --> 02:17:25,699
And James doing the opposite to what he did in the synchro.

1638
02:17:25,718 --> 02:17:28,102
In the synchro, he went over, over a vertical.

1639
02:17:28,163 --> 02:17:29,525
Here he is slightly short.

1640
02:17:29,685 --> 02:17:31,588
In fact, he is quite short.

1641
02:17:31,770 --> 02:17:32,591
Who am I trying to kid?

1642
02:17:32,630 --> 02:17:37,840
He's landing pretty much on the backs of his legs, going loose in the lower back.

1643
02:17:37,879 --> 02:17:39,423
It is such a difficult dive.

1644
02:17:39,442 --> 02:17:42,608
And when it goes wrong, it can go drastically wrong.

1645
02:17:43,667 --> 02:17:45,750
He will drop down the leaderboard with that one.

1646
02:17:46,490 --> 02:17:51,457
Well, apart from Lee, everybody else is having problems with that dive in different configurations.

1647
02:17:52,477 --> 02:17:54,320
Including James Denny.

1648
02:17:54,380 --> 02:18:00,407
He's at 48.6 and more and more it's looking like there's not going to be as much pressure as we thought on Tom Daley.

1649
02:18:02,309 --> 02:18:06,854
I would say Liang was there or there about, but he had a four second Ryan dive.

1650
02:18:06,875 --> 02:18:10,840
So he needs to get it back on track with a fourth, three and a half with Pike.

1651
02:18:14,514 --> 02:18:15,736
That is back on track.

1652
02:18:15,755 --> 02:18:17,358
It's very good for Moutilier.

1653
02:18:18,559 --> 02:18:20,262
His easiest dive, 3.0.

1654
02:18:20,662 --> 02:18:22,404
Forward, three and a half in the pike position.

1655
02:18:22,443 --> 02:18:24,126
Such a strong athlete.

1656
02:18:24,146 --> 02:18:25,308
Leaps off the diving board.

1657
02:18:26,088 --> 02:18:27,549
Just rolling into the water.

1658
02:18:27,569 --> 02:18:28,592
He's going to get eights on that.

1659
02:18:28,631 --> 02:18:29,333
That'll help him.

1660
02:18:30,593 --> 02:18:33,057
Will he see himself top of the leaderboard?

1661
02:18:34,359 --> 02:18:34,918
Yes.

1662
02:18:34,939 --> 02:18:35,819
For the time being, he will.

1663
02:18:36,240 --> 02:18:37,843
First to go over the 200 mark.

1664
02:18:37,862 --> 02:18:39,844
208, to be precise.

1665
02:18:39,905 --> 02:18:43,189
Nine clear of Lee and 17 ahead of Bedcourt.

1666
02:18:45,210 --> 02:18:48,354
The main movers and shakers are about to perform.

1667
02:18:48,375 --> 02:18:51,440
At the halfway stage approaching.

1668
02:18:53,503 --> 02:18:58,469
Future of Canadian male 10 meter diving has arrived in Edinburgh.

1669
02:18:59,710 --> 02:19:04,618
Let's see whether he accepts that tag gratefully and gladly on this reverse.

1670
02:19:04,778 --> 02:19:09,023
Three and a half somersaults with tuck 3.4 attached to this.

1671
02:19:10,967 --> 02:19:12,349
Oh, he's taking it on.

1672
02:19:12,886 --> 02:19:18,578
Yeah, the Canadians, both of them, both Vincent and Maxime to follow shortly.

1673
02:19:20,884 --> 02:19:22,066
Wow, good dives.

1674
02:19:22,527 --> 02:19:24,592
This one in particular, 3.4.

1675
02:19:24,611 --> 02:19:25,173
It's tricky.

1676
02:19:25,774 --> 02:19:26,717
Get it all the way around.

1677
02:19:28,480 --> 02:19:30,424
Anything above 70 points is good.

1678
02:19:30,465 --> 02:19:32,328
75 points, even better.

1679
02:19:33,018 --> 02:19:35,602
Then up into the higher echelons we go.

1680
02:19:36,002 --> 02:19:40,189
I would not be at all surprised if this young man isn't on the podium later on today.

1681
02:19:40,488 --> 02:19:44,013
Started with great confidence, started with a great smile, started with a great attitude.

1682
02:19:44,033 --> 02:19:48,139
It might well be a battle between the Canadians for medals here.

1683
02:19:50,644 --> 02:19:52,527
Or is it not going to be Matt Mitchum's night?

1684
02:19:52,826 --> 02:19:56,072
Perhaps two of them could sneak on to the medal podium.

1685
02:19:57,924 --> 02:20:03,713
Simon Bouchard is not too far shy of a top three place, in fact, with everybody else faltering.

1686
02:20:04,854 --> 02:20:07,519
Time for him to step up on that 3.4.

1687
02:20:07,780 --> 02:20:10,664
So we have some big tariff dives to come.

1688
02:20:10,824 --> 02:20:13,908
They get more immense as the competition goes on.

1689
02:20:14,930 --> 02:20:16,413
This is mid-range, really.

1690
02:20:16,772 --> 02:20:17,713
Not for Bouchard, though.

1691
02:20:18,174 --> 02:20:23,442
Reverse three and a half somersaults with Tuck for the second of the Canadians.

1692
02:20:38,542 --> 02:20:39,924
Oh, it's an unusual technique.

1693
02:20:39,944 --> 02:20:42,868
He's balancing on his tiptoes, but he's standing forwards.

1694
02:20:42,907 --> 02:20:43,969
That's highly unusual.

1695
02:20:43,989 --> 02:20:45,512
He took ages to go as well.

1696
02:20:46,092 --> 02:20:50,016
It's exactly the same dive as his teammate Vincent has just performed, and it's not as good.

1697
02:20:51,199 --> 02:20:57,647
So that means that Max will drop a little bit further away from where he was on the previous round.

1698
02:20:59,148 --> 02:21:01,791
He only needed seven and a halfs and eights, but that's only going to get 5.5s.

1699
02:21:01,811 --> 02:21:05,816
24 points behind his teammate now.

1700
02:21:06,825 --> 02:21:08,727
Three rounds ago, that can be made up.

1701
02:21:10,591 --> 02:21:17,539
But Liandau is setting the pace amongst the... Well, it looked like being the lesser medalist now.

1702
02:21:17,779 --> 02:21:22,704
Round three this morning was a very good dive for Matt Mitchum on his reverse three and a half.

1703
02:21:23,605 --> 02:21:25,509
That's his best dive of the competition.

1704
02:21:25,529 --> 02:21:30,774
88.4 he got, but he's down on his first two dives tonight.

1705
02:21:35,816 --> 02:21:37,498
Oh, it's a good dive for Mitchen.

1706
02:21:37,519 --> 02:21:39,220
He manages to keep the splash down.

1707
02:21:39,601 --> 02:21:41,863
It is the rip entry that we're looking for.

1708
02:21:42,465 --> 02:21:45,007
He does wash over a vertical.

1709
02:21:45,028 --> 02:21:48,592
So he's only going to get, well, eight and a halfs maybe.

1710
02:21:49,433 --> 02:21:56,981
He needed to be completely bolt upright to get nine and a halfs and tens, which is pretty much what he would need to put pressure on Tom Daley.

1711
02:21:57,402 --> 02:21:58,824
This is a big, big dive though.

1712
02:21:58,843 --> 02:22:00,845
85 points plus.

1713
02:22:02,006 --> 02:22:04,069
Well, he got 450 total this morning.

1714
02:22:04,611 --> 02:22:04,970
He's happy.

1715
02:22:04,990 --> 02:22:07,513
A little jig of joy and delight for Matt Mitchum.

1716
02:22:07,534 --> 02:22:10,599
Well, he's come close to emulating what he did this morning.

1717
02:22:10,818 --> 02:22:12,060
Still hasn't quite done it.

1718
02:22:13,423 --> 02:22:17,288
In terms of tariff, the weakest dive for Tom Daley.

1719
02:22:17,788 --> 02:22:20,252
Doesn't always translate into execution.

1720
02:22:22,013 --> 02:22:22,555
It will be though.

1721
02:22:23,195 --> 02:22:27,762
Any moment now, an inward three and a half somersaults with tuck for Daley.

1722
02:22:27,909 --> 02:22:42,038
takeoff is electric he's been working so hard on this boom on the start really good strong start just rolling over as he goes into the water he's going to get eight and a half's probably not good enough for a nine

1723
02:22:42,406 --> 02:22:43,307
Good enough, though.

1724
02:22:43,346 --> 02:22:44,667
He'll be over 80 points.

1725
02:22:44,688 --> 02:22:51,915
81.6, and he knows in his head how that compares with this morning.

1726
02:22:52,296 --> 02:22:53,996
Not that favorably.

1727
02:22:54,518 --> 02:22:57,640
81.6, but 83 points this morning.

1728
02:22:57,900 --> 02:23:00,202
So first time on his evening performance.

1729
02:23:00,222 --> 02:23:02,165
He's down on marks, but it's only marginal.

1730
02:23:02,906 --> 02:23:04,768
Tom Daly, Vincent Riendoe.

1731
02:23:05,208 --> 02:23:09,072
Mitchum has woken up and come to the party now in third place.

1732
02:23:09,929 --> 02:23:18,002
It would say Liang in fourth and the two other Englishmen in the field, James Denny in eighth and Matt Dixon in tenth.

1733
02:23:19,623 --> 02:23:20,685
So we've reached halfway.

1734
02:23:21,165 --> 02:23:28,297
It's looking good for Tom Daly with a 26 point gap between him and the rest right now.

1735
02:23:28,698 --> 02:23:30,120
But we are only halfway.

1736
02:23:30,139 --> 02:23:37,371
As I mentioned, the big dives, not for the likes of Siddharth Padeshi, but the main divers still to come.

1737
02:23:38,272 --> 02:23:38,333
OK.

1738
02:23:40,050 --> 02:23:41,173
28 seconds last time.

1739
02:23:42,754 --> 02:23:44,817
How long will you take over this one?

1740
02:23:46,059 --> 02:23:48,343
Reverse two and a half somersaults with Pike.

1741
02:23:50,947 --> 02:23:52,129
Still not quite ready to go.

1742
02:23:52,148 --> 02:24:04,165
So your TV hasn't frozen.

1743
02:24:04,586 --> 02:24:05,247
This is actually happening.

1744
02:24:11,370 --> 02:24:17,778
Well, next to me in the radio section, Karen Pickering has summed it up perfectly.

1745
02:24:17,798 --> 02:24:25,406
She shifted back in a chair and held herself because it doesn't tickle hitting the water at over 35 miles an hour.

1746
02:24:25,425 --> 02:24:28,529
And when you don't get anywhere near up by, that really does hurt.

1747
02:24:28,549 --> 02:24:31,252
You can tell why Siddhartha was taking his time and having to think about it.

1748
02:24:31,712 --> 02:24:32,533
It's a tricky dive.

1749
02:24:32,554 --> 02:24:34,274
Reverse two and a half in the pike position.

1750
02:24:34,976 --> 02:24:37,699
And he's just had the rough of the water.

1751
02:24:38,253 --> 02:24:39,976
This man made a steal or what?

1752
02:24:40,075 --> 02:24:54,520
He was doing something similar in the build-up and the training before the event itself and just took the knocks, got back on that 10-meter board, did it all over again, but no improvement from the practice, I'm afraid.

1753
02:24:56,643 --> 02:24:59,808
Matt Dixon is not too put off by that.

1754
02:24:59,827 --> 02:25:03,854
3.2 for the youngster.

1755
02:25:04,932 --> 02:25:10,485
He has senior debut at the Commonwealth Games, in with three and a half somersaults, 3.2.

1756
02:25:12,168 --> 02:25:13,872
He's probably safe from finishing bottom.

1757
02:25:14,212 --> 02:25:16,257
Let's see if he can make a few strides up with this.

1758
02:25:26,566 --> 02:25:31,671
What a dive from the 14-year-old from Plymouth.

1759
02:25:31,691 --> 02:25:34,654
He's absolutely smashed it.

1760
02:25:35,635 --> 02:25:35,835
Wow.

1761
02:25:37,217 --> 02:25:39,119
That is what he's capable of.

1762
02:25:40,479 --> 02:25:42,462
They've got some big scores coming his way.

1763
02:25:43,042 --> 02:25:44,645
I am liking that.

1764
02:25:45,445 --> 02:25:47,186
Good work, Matty Dixon.

1765
02:25:51,412 --> 02:25:55,476
Well, physically, he might look out of place here, but those marks aren't.

1766
02:25:56,299 --> 02:26:00,525
8.5, 8.5, 8.5, 81.6.

1767
02:26:01,746 --> 02:26:02,468
My oh my.

1768
02:26:02,968 --> 02:26:04,310
I did say he's not going to finish bottom.

1769
02:26:04,511 --> 02:26:07,194
He may well be a couple of places above that.

1770
02:26:07,614 --> 02:26:08,836
The performances of that kind.

1771
02:26:08,897 --> 02:26:11,560
That is sensational from the young man.

1772
02:26:12,002 --> 02:26:14,825
Just shows the promise he has down in Plymouth.

1773
02:26:14,885 --> 02:26:17,709
Andy Banks working so hard with him and the others.

1774
02:26:17,909 --> 02:26:18,790
Great little program.

1775
02:26:19,711 --> 02:26:23,336
Andy, of course, worked for 12 years with Tom Daly before he moved to London.

1776
02:26:24,903 --> 02:26:26,966
That's what special coaches do.

1777
02:26:29,831 --> 02:26:35,138
Chu Yue in with three and a half somersaults with Tuck, three point two for the Malaysian.

1778
02:26:35,899 --> 02:26:37,502
Wrong end of the field in ninth at the moment.

1779
02:26:38,844 --> 02:26:40,105
Oh, it's better from Chu Yue.

1780
02:26:40,606 --> 02:26:46,777
Yeah, his third round dive, the back three and a half when he went surfing cost him his spot on the leaderboard.

1781
02:26:46,797 --> 02:26:47,597
This is better.

1782
02:26:48,019 --> 02:26:50,843
Not as good as Matty Dixon, but not far off.

1783
02:26:52,611 --> 02:26:53,293
Strong takeoff.

1784
02:26:53,314 --> 02:26:55,379
She used to use a towel, that's a comfort thing.

1785
02:26:56,082 --> 02:27:04,747
It's a non-slip surface on the platform and some divers prefer the grip of a towel, which is the blue towel that you saw on the 10 meter there, just as Chiu Yue was performing his dive.

1786
02:27:05,773 --> 02:27:06,475
76.80.

1787
02:27:06,594 --> 02:27:10,801
Doesn't look to me like he's going to be pushing for a medal.

1788
02:27:11,442 --> 02:27:15,449
Stay with big tariff times, which can easily be dropped or failed on occasion.

1789
02:27:16,990 --> 02:27:20,675
Can't always make that prediction even at this stage, but two rounds to go.

1790
02:27:20,695 --> 02:27:22,638
Looks like he's not going to be in the shakeup.

1791
02:27:23,800 --> 02:27:27,126
This man still could be a bit in and out.

1792
02:27:27,566 --> 02:27:34,137
Great start in both the prelims and the final for Dominic Hedgood.

1793
02:27:34,156 --> 02:27:35,038
3.4.

1794
02:27:35,305 --> 02:27:36,505
Reverse three and a half.

1795
02:27:37,086 --> 02:27:39,370
60 will put him above Chuyui.

1796
02:27:40,490 --> 02:27:43,293
He'll be looking, though, for 80s if he can.

1797
02:27:48,340 --> 02:27:50,082
Well, it's better from Bedgood.

1798
02:27:50,903 --> 02:27:51,763
Better from Bedgood.

1799
02:27:54,406 --> 02:27:55,827
This went to Rai in the prelims.

1800
02:27:56,588 --> 02:27:58,351
He almost gets it right here in the final.

1801
02:27:58,370 --> 02:28:00,173
He just needs to look back a little bit more.

1802
02:28:01,395 --> 02:28:03,076
Marginally short vertical as he goes in.

1803
02:28:03,096 --> 02:28:04,417
It's still a good dive.

1804
02:28:04,870 --> 02:28:06,210
way over 70 points.

1805
02:28:07,692 --> 02:28:08,953
Where will that put him?

1806
02:28:08,974 --> 02:28:29,115
76.5 is what he gets in terms of total marks and for the time being he keeps changing hands as it always does at this stage as divers just get their noses in front of the opposition but we're not down to the sharp end by any means yet.

1807
02:28:29,236 --> 02:28:32,379
Seven divers to go and

1808
02:28:32,916 --> 02:28:36,724
Both Lee and James Denny will be performing that dive.

1809
02:28:37,364 --> 02:28:40,470
Reverse three and a half somersaults with tuck 3.4.

1810
02:28:42,655 --> 02:28:48,105
Lee looking to go crashing through the 200 barrier here, currently in fifth place.

1811
02:28:48,146 --> 02:28:53,675
So again, not too far shy of a top three place.

1812
02:28:55,123 --> 02:28:57,085
Yes, he is.

1813
02:28:57,105 --> 02:28:59,128
It just goes to show how difficult these dives are.

1814
02:28:59,147 --> 02:29:02,170
This one in particular, the reverse three and a half.

1815
02:29:02,190 --> 02:29:08,215
He's got to jump away from the diving board, spin backwards towards it, which is exactly what Lee does.

1816
02:29:08,255 --> 02:29:13,260
He's just squeezing his shape in there, comes out if he's diving a little bit too early, lands flat on his back.

1817
02:29:14,380 --> 02:29:14,941
What a shame.

1818
02:29:15,422 --> 02:29:23,629
Yeah, it looks like his chance of a medal, which looked very good before that dive.

1819
02:29:23,962 --> 02:29:27,906
have just evaporated at the Royal Commonwealth call in Edinburgh.

1820
02:29:28,406 --> 02:29:33,191
Former Chinese diver, retired, came back coaching in Wellington.

1821
02:29:34,572 --> 02:29:39,457
I think he is still coaching as well as well as performing, but the person who decided retirement was not for him.

1822
02:29:40,878 --> 02:29:44,320
Consideration retirement for this man, 20 years of age.

1823
02:29:44,480 --> 02:29:49,845
